description:
Part 1 of 6 of omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3 (Schemas with the serialize contract, declared `details`, and live validation). If this is the last open subtask of that bead, verify its acceptance criteria and close it as its body says.

## Background

The parent leaf makes omaddons' JSON output describe itself truthfully: a draft 2020-12 JSON Schema for every command's `data`, the envelope, every stderr NDJSON event and every persisted file, generated with schemars' **serialize** contract and one fresh generator per schema (M4-D9), an error schema that types every code's `details` (M4-D10), strict validation of live output in the contract suite, and a rule test that holds every shape to the contract's naming rules (M4-D55). A5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.5`, `robot-docs schema`) publishes these schemas, A4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.4`, `capabilities`) points at them, and A10 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.10`, the semantic manifest) pins them.

This part generates the schemas: a new `src/contract/schema.rs` with the generator settings and one function per kind of schema, `JsonSchema` on `Envelope` and `Meta`, `store::KINDS` rows that carry their file's schema, and a documentation-only schema for `addons.toml` held equal to its parser's keys. It changes no output byte. It is its own step because everything after it (the error union of subtask 2, `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3.2`; the validation of subtask 4, `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3.4`) reads these functions, and because it needs no validator: it can land in parallel with subtask 3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3.3`, the dev-dependency and the strict transform).

Why the serialize contract and fresh generators (M4-D9): schemars derives the *deserialize* contract by default, under which every field without `#[serde(default)]` is required; there are 96 `skip_serializing_if` sites in `src/`, mostly `-v`-only fields, so every real output that omits one would fail. Under `for_serialize()` (schemars 1.2.3 crate source `src/generate.rs:183`) a field is optional exactly when it has `skip_serializing_if`. schemars also names duplicate type names by generation order (`Summary`, `Summary2`, … `src/generate.rs:337-346`) and copies every definition a generator has seen into each root (`src/generate.rs:466`), so a generator shared by two schemas makes one's `$defs` depend on the other. Rejected: one generator for all (unstable names), `serde_json/preserve_order` for declaration-order properties (dozens of snapshots change for a cosmetic gain; property order in a schema means nothing).

**Facts it relies on** (`c0ab5e9`, plus the blocking leaves):
- `trait Outcome { type Data: Serialize + schemars::JsonSchema; … }` (`src/output/mod.rs:34-35`); about 403 `JsonSchema` derives in `src/`; `schemars = "1.2.3"` with default features (`Cargo.toml:24`).
- A1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.1`): every `app::COMMANDS` row has `data: fn(&mut SchemaGenerator) -> Schema` (`data_schema::<O>()` = `g.root_schema_for::<O::Data>()`), and `ENVELOPE_ONLY` holds `omaddons` and `version`, each with `data`. `app::command_entry(path)` looks a row up.
- A2 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.2`): `src/contract/` exists (`pub mod contract;` in `src/lib.rs`); `src/contract/events.rs` has the four event structs with `JsonSchema`, `EventName::ALL`, `EventName::wire()` and `EventName::schema(g)`.
- `Envelope<'a, D: Serialize>` and `Meta` (`src/output/envelope.rs:13-38`) derive `Serialize` only. `Envelope.data: Option<&'a D>` has no doc comment; `partial` says "Present whenever the command produced data." and `error` "Present iff `ok` is false."
- `store::KINDS: &[(&str, SchemaVersion)]` (`src/state/store.rs:107-185`): 19 `Versioned` rows (`<T as Versioned>::KIND`, `::CURRENT`) and `("history", super::history::CURRENT)`. Only `store.rs` reads it; its test `every_persisted_format_has_a_kinds_row` (`:435-452`) finds each `impl Versioned for T` in `production_code` and requires the text `::{T} as Versioned>::KIND` among the rows. `trait Versioned: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + JsonSchema` (`:89-102`). `encode` (`:320-334`) writes `Document { schema_version: T::CURRENT, #[serde(flatten)] value }` (a function-local struct); `SchemaVersion` is `#[serde(try_from = "String", into = "String")]` (`:27-32`).
- `JournalLine` (`src/engine/journal.rs:49-60`) derives `Serialize, JsonSchema`, `#[serde(tag = "type")]`. `HistoryEntry` (`src/state/history.rs:30-68`) derives `JsonSchema` and carries `schema_version`.
- `addons.toml` is parsed with `toml::de::DeTable` (`src/state/desired.rs:37`); the keys it knows are match-arm literals only: the file's `schema_version`, `family`, `target` (`:189-195`), a section's `addons`, `addon` (`:392-397`), an entry's `name`, `ref`, `version`, `channel`, `pinned`, `dependency`, `sha256`, `revision`, `any_flavor` (`:467-498`); every other key goes to `unknown_key` (`:283-298`), which warns `desired_unknown_key`. (The plan says `toml_edit` and "the parser's known-key lists"; neither is true at `c0ab5e9`, so this part adds the lists.) `Family` derives `JsonSchema` with `rename_all = "kebab-case"` (`src/rules.rs:145-149`); `Family::ALL` (`:176`) includes `Family::Unknown` (`:163`), which `parse` refuses. `Channel` derives `JsonSchema` with `rename_all = "lowercase"` (`src/model.rs:386-402`).
- `src/source_scan.rs` (`production_code`, `sources`) is available to unit tests in `src/` (`#[cfg(test)]`, `src/lib.rs:37-38`).

## Technical Approach

### 1. `src/contract/schema.rs`

Declared from `src/contract/mod.rs` (`pub mod schema;`). A5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.5`, `robot-docs schema`) publishes what these functions return. Module doc: what the module publishes, M4-D9 in two sentences, and that published schemas are open (strictness is the contract suite's test-side transform).

```rust
/// The settings every published schema is generated with (M4-D9).
pub fn settings() -> SchemaSettings { SchemaSettings::draft2020_12().for_serialize() }
/// A fresh generator: one per root, never reused, so `$defs` names depend on one type only.
pub fn generator() -> SchemaGenerator { settings().into_generator() }

/// One command's `data` schema, `title` = the command path.
pub fn command_schema(entry: &CommandEntry) -> Schema;
/// Every `app::COMMANDS` row's, keyed by path (A5 publishes this map as `commands`).
pub fn command_schemas() -> BTreeMap<&'static str, Schema>;
/// The `data` schema for an envelope `command`: a `COMMANDS` row's, else an `ENVELOPE_ONLY`
/// name's (`omaddons`, `version`), else `None`.
pub fn data_schema_for(command: &str) -> Option<Schema>;
/// The envelope's: `Envelope<'static, serde_json::Value>`, so `data` is open (each command's own
/// schema describes it); `error` is `ErrorBody`'s schema.
pub fn envelope_schema() -> Schema;
/// One per `EventName::ALL`, keyed by wire name, `event` pinned with `const`.
pub fn event_schemas() -> BTreeMap<&'static str, Schema>;
/// Every persisted format: each `store::KINDS` row, `journal` and `desired_state`.
pub fn file_schemas() -> BTreeMap<&'static str, Schema>;
```

- Every function builds each root with `generator()`; none takes or keeps a generator.
- `command_schema` sets `title` to `entry.name` (schemars sets it to the Rust type name, which is not a stable identifier). `file_schemas` sets each root's `title` to its key, and `desired_state`'s `description` names the file `addons.toml`.
- `event_schemas` replaces each schema's `properties.event` with `{"type":"string","const":"<wire>"}`, so a published warning event can never validate as an error event. Decided while writing this bead (A2's (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.2`, the action and event registries) bead left the pin to this one).
- `data_schema_for` exists because envelopes name two commands that are no clap path; the contract suite (subtask 4) uses it to pick the schema of any envelope.
- Determinism: `serde_json` without `preserve_order` sorts object keys; `required` arrays keep field order, which is fixed per build. Two calls give byte-identical JSON.

### 2. The envelope

In `src/output/envelope.rs`:

- `Envelope` derives `JsonSchema` with `#[schemars(rename = "Envelope")]` (the generic would otherwise be named `Envelope_for_AnyValue`); schemars adds the `D: JsonSchema` bound itself. `Meta` derives `JsonSchema`.
- `data` gains the doc comment "Omitted on a failure, except an exit-6 assertion failure (`--check`, `--strict`), which keeps it." (rule 2 of M4-D55 requires every omittable key to say when it is omitted; subtask 5's rule test reads descriptions).
- The `error` field's schema is `ErrorBody`'s. Until subtask 2 replaces `ErrorBody`'s derive with the code union, it is the derived one (with `details` open); `envelope_schema()` picks the union up with no change here.
- No byte of any envelope changes; the envelope snapshots under `src/output/snapshots/` and `tests/` pass unchanged.

### 3. `store::KINDS` rows that carry their schema

In `src/state/store.rs`:

```rust
/// One persisted format: its name, the version this build writes, and the schema of what it writes.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub struct KindRow {
    pub kind: &'static str,
    pub current: SchemaVersion,
    pub schema: fn(&mut SchemaGenerator) -> Schema,
}
impl KindRow {
    pub const fn of<T: Versioned>() -> Self {
        Self { kind: T::KIND, current: T::CURRENT, schema: <T as Versioned>::schema }
    }
}
pub const KINDS: &[KindRow] = &[
    KindRow::of::<super::records::TargetRecord>(),
    // … the 18 other Versioned rows, in today's order …
    KindRow { kind: "history", current: super::history::CURRENT, schema: super::history::line_schema },
];
```

- `Versioned` gains a provided method: `fn schema(g: &mut SchemaGenerator) -> Schema where Self: Sized + 'static { g.root_schema_for::<Document<'static, Self>>() }`, documented as "the schema of the document `save` writes: `schema_version` first, then this type's fields". No `Versioned` impl changes.
- `Document` moves from inside `encode` to module scope and derives `JsonSchema` too: `#[derive(Serialize, JsonSchema)] struct Document<'a, T> { schema_version: SchemaVersion, #[serde(flatten)] value: &'a T }`. `encode` keeps using it, so the file's bytes and its schema come from one type. `encode`'s output is byte-identical (the store's existing tests prove it).
- `src/state/history.rs` gains `pub fn line_schema(g: &mut SchemaGenerator) -> Schema { g.root_schema_for::<HistoryEntry>() }` ("one line of `history.jsonl`").
- `every_persisted_format_has_a_kinds_row` changes only its row match: `rows.contains(&format!("::{name}>()"))` (the `KindRow::of::<…::Name>()` form), keeping the count check `found.len() + 1 == KINDS.len()` and the `release_memo`/`http_validators` presence check (`KINDS.iter().map(|r| r.kind)`).
- The `const fn of` builds a function pointer from a generic associated function; that is allowed in `const fn` on the pinned toolchain (1.97). If the compiler refuses it, make `KINDS` a `static` built the same way and record it.
- Later leaves add rows in this form: D4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.4`) `plan`, E3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.5.3`) `doctor_report` (a non-`Versioned` row with its own schema function, like `history`), E5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.5.5`) `repair_journal`. A row a peer added in the tuple form before this part lands is converted here.

