**`src/resolve/cache.rs`** (using the existing fakes in its test module: `Fake`, `cache(policy)`, `once`, `later`, and `trace::capture`)
- `each_memo_decision_is_traced`: one case per row of section 6's per-wish table: `fresh_window`, `offline_remembered`, `stale_window_probes`, `revalidate_probes`, `remembered_failure_fetches`, `no_probe_token_fetches`, `refresh_fetches`, `offline_unremembered`, `not_remembered`, `pinned_version`, `transient_cache`, `local_ref`, `url_ref`, `answered_earlier_in_the_run`. Each asserts the captured line's prefix and decision words exactly, and that the age or window figures are numbers.
- `probes_and_fetches_are_traced_with_their_time`: a stale entry whose probe token is unchanged gives `release probe … token unchanged … ms)`; a changed token gives `token changed, fetching`, then the `release fetch:` batch line and the per-wish `newest` line; a probe error gives `failed (<code>)`. Each timing parses as an integer.
- `decision_line_never_names_a_local_or_url_ref`: for a `local:` ref with a path and a `url:` ref with a query string, no captured line contains the path or the query.

**`src/discover/mod.rs`**
- `each_root_is_traced_with_the_route_that_reached_it_first`: two `Candidates::add` calls for the same tempdir (canonicalizable), the first with a `product_db` route, the second with a `scan` route: the captured lines are the "first route to reach it" line for `product_db`, then the "already reached by product_db; hints merged" line for `scan`. A third add for another tempdir gives its own "first route" line.
- `route_labels`: `product_db` with qualifier `battlenet` → `product_db (battlenet)`; `launcher lutris` with qualifier `lutris` → `launcher lutris (lutris)`; `scan` with an empty qualifier → `scan`.

**`src/fsx/lock.rs`** (on a tempdir `Paths`, with `trace::capture` on the acquiring thread)
- `an_uncontended_acquire_is_traced_at_once`: the lines are exactly `["global lock: acquired at once"]`.
- `a_contended_acquire_traces_the_wait_and_its_end`: a helper thread acquires the lock as command `holder`, signals over a channel that it holds it, and drops it 100 ms later; once signalled, the main thread's `acquire_with_timeout(.., 2 s)` captures a `held by omaddons holder (pid <this pid>, since …); waiting up to 2000 ms` line, then `acquired after <n> ms (<k> retries)` with `n ≥ 50` and `k ≥ 1`.
- `a_timed_out_acquire_traces_the_wait_only`: with the lock held for the whole test, `acquire_with_timeout(.., 60 ms)` returns `locked` and the lines are the `… waiting up to 60 ms` line, then `global lock: not acquired within 60 ms`, and no `acquired after` line.

**`src/cli.rs`**
- `a_repeated_v_counts_within_one_command_level`: `Cli::try_parse_from` over `omaddons` plus: `-v` → 1, `-vv` → 2, `-v -v` → 2, `--verbose --verbose` → 2, `status -vv` → 2, `-vvv status` → 3, `-v status -v` → 1, `-v backup -v list -v` → 1. The message on failure says README's Global options row must change with it.

### Integration and end-to-end tests

Decided while writing this bead: two suites. The level-1 characterization lives in the contract suite (`tests/contract/verbosity.rs`), because its rows then run through `check()` and `stable()` like every matrix row and are validated by A3's live schemas; the multi-command scenarios live in `tests/e2e_verbosity.rs`, whose `e2e_` prefix is what `argc e2e` selects.

**`tests/contract/verbosity.rs`** (new module of the contract suite, `mod verbosity;` in `tests/contract/main.rs`; commit 1). Every run goes through the suite's `check()`, so every stdout and stderr line meets the whole contract, and once A3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3`, the schemas and their live validation) has landed every stderr line, trace lines included, is validated against its event schema.

- `level_one_output_is_characterized`: for each of the 15 files of the 17 sites, take that command's success row from `tests/contract/matrix.rs`, run it with `-v` added on the same kind of `Scene` (`Scene::new()`, plus `s.install_foo()`, and `s.dependencies()` with LittleWigs installed so a dependency exists), and snapshot `s.stable(&envelope)` as `verbosity_<command>_v` (for example `verbosity_status_v`, `verbosity_list_v`, `verbosity_info_v`, `verbosity_undo_dry_run_v`). Where the matrix row is a real run (`install`, `adopt`), run it once on a fresh scene. The rows: `status`, `list`, `targets`, `history -t retail`, `info gh:o/foo`, `outdated`, `backup list`, `errors`, `undo <tx> --dry-run`, `pin foo -t retail --dry-run`, `update -t retail --dry-run`, `copy` (the matrix's success argv, `--dry-run`), `sync` (the matrix's success argv, `--dry-run`), `adopt` (the matrix's success argv) and `install` (the matrix's success argv). Where a row needs a fixture the scene lacks, build it with the existing `common` builders and say so in the module doc.
- `level_one_human_output_is_characterized`: `list -v` (exercising `list.rs:429`, the client dir, and `list.rs:448`, "dependency of LittleWigs"), `info gh:o/foo -v` (`info.rs:332`'s compat lines), `outdated -v` and `status -v`, without `--json`, with the tempdir replaced by `<root>` and any wall-clock or relative time replaced as the suite's `redact` does, snapshotted as `verbosity_<command>_v_human`. A row whose human text cannot be made stable is dropped, and the close comment says which and why.
- `json_stdout_is_identical_at_v_and_vv`: for every read-only and `--dry-run` row above, run `-v` then `-vv` on the same home and assert `without_meta(stdout)` is equal; for the two real-run rows, run `-v` on one fresh scene and `-vv` on another and assert their `s.stable()` forms are equal. For every `-vv` run, assert that each stderr line whose `event` is `log` has a `level` in `info | debug | trace`, and that the `-v` run has no `trace` line.
- `human_stdout_is_identical_at_v_and_vv`: the human rows above, compared byte for byte after the same redaction.

**`tests/e2e_verbosity.rs`** (new end-to-end suite; `argc e2e verbosity` runs it with verbose logs). Each scenario is a `TestLog` scenario (`let log = tlog!();`) on a fresh `common::home::Home`, every command run through `log.run` (with the `Home`'s `OMADDONS_HTTP_FIXTURES`, and for paused children `OMADDONS_FAILPOINTS` and `OMADDONS_FAILPOINT_DIR`, as recorded environment overrides), with `--progress json` so stderr is NDJSON. A helper `trace_lines(&Ran) -> Vec<String>` returns the messages of the `log` events whose `level` is `trace`, and asserts each such event has exactly the keys `event`, `level`, `message`.

1. `trace_events_appear_only_at_vv_and_only_on_stderr`: `Home::new(&["wow"])` with `common::wtf::Wtf::at(home.client("_retail_"))` holding SavedVariables for the fake account, realm and character.
   - step `first run at -vv`: `status -vv --json` → exit 0; at least one trace line starts with `discovery route ` and names the Battle.net root (`World of Warcraft`), and at least one starts with `discovery root ` and ends with `parsed`.
   - step `warm run at -vv`: `log.tree("state", <state>)` and `log.tree("cache", <cache>)` (the first run wrote the discovery cache under `<cache>`; `status` writes nothing else, `src/app/status.rs:4`); `status -vv --json` → a `discovery root … reused from the discovery cache` line.
   - step `warm run at -v`: `status -v --json` → at least one `debug` line (`discovery: scanned yes, …`), no trace line; its envelope without `meta` equals the previous step's.
   - step `default`: `status --json` → no `debug` and no trace line, and the level-1 field `client_dir`, which the `-v` run's `data` carries for the retail client, is absent (it is `skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none"`, `src/app/status.rs:245-247`).
   - step `quiet`: `status --quiet -vv --json` → no `log` event of any level; stdout without `meta` equals the `-vv` run's.
   - step `forms`: `-v -v status`, `--verbose --verbose status` and `status -vv` each give at least one trace line; `-v status -v` gives none and at least one `debug` line.
   - step `cached`: `status --cached -vv --json` → `discovery root … reused` lines and no `discovery route` line.
   - step `nothing written`: `log.assert_unchanged("state", <state>)` and `log.assert_unchanged("cache", <cache>)` across the warm steps.
   - every step: `assert_private_all(stdout, stderr)`, and no trace message contains `WTF/`.
2. `the_release_memo_traces_each_decision_and_its_timing`: `Home::new(&["wow"])` and `gh_release(&home.http, "https://github.com/o/foo", "v1", …)` (as `tests/release_cache.rs`'s `foo` helper builds it).
   - step `not remembered`: `info gh:o/foo -vv --json` → `release memo gh:o/foo|stable: not remembered, fetching`, a `release fetch: 1 ref from 1 source in <n> ms` line and `release fetch gh:o/foo|stable: newest v1 …, remembered`; `net.log` gained at least one line (T1, `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.1`, records the lines added).
   - step `fresh`: the same command → `… fresh, answered from the memo (fetched <s> s ago, window 900 s); no request`; `net.log` gained nothing.
   - step `fresh at -v`: `info gh:o/foo -v --json` → no trace line; envelope without `meta` equals the previous step's.
   - step `offline`: `info gh:o/foo -vv --offline --json` → `… offline, answered from the memo whatever its age …`.
   - step `refresh`: `info gh:o/foo -vv --refresh --json` → `… --refresh, fetching` and a `release fetch:` batch line.
   - step `stale, same token`: `home.seed_memo(&memo::of(vec![memo::entry("gh:o/foo", "v1", memo::ago(20))]))`, then `info gh:o/foo -vv --json` → `… stale (fetched <s> s ago), probing the source` with `s ≥ 1200`, then `release probe gh:o/foo|stable: token unchanged, kept the remembered set (<n> ms)`.
   - step `stale, moved tag`: seed `v0` at 20 minutes ago (as `an_aged_entry_is_confirmed_by_one_request_and_fresh_again` does), then `info gh:o/foo -vv --json` → `release probe …: token changed, fetching (<n> ms)` and the fetch lines with `newest v1`.
   - every step: `assert_private_all`.
3. `a_lock_wait_is_traced_while_it_waits`: `Home::new(&["wow"])` and a `common::pause::Pause` in the home.
   - step `uncontended`: `config set check_interval_hours 6 -vv --json` → exit 0 and the trace line `global lock: acquired at once`; at `-v` the same command gives no trace line.
   - step `holder pauses`: spawn `config set check_interval_hours 12 --json` with `OMADDONS_FAILPOINTS=fsx.lock.holder_written=pause` and the pause dir (`home.spawn`); `pause.reached("fsx.lock.holder_written")`.
   - step `waiter traces the wait`: spawn `config set check_interval_hours 24 -vv` (`home.spawn`, stderr piped); a reader thread sends each stderr line over a channel; the test waits (at most 4 s, under the 5 s `LOCK_ACQUIRE_TIMEOUT`) for a trace line starting `global lock: held by omaddons config set (pid <holder pid>` and ending `waiting up to 5000 ms`, and logs it with `log.json`. Only then: `pause.resume("fsx.lock.holder_written")`.
   - step `both finish`: the holder exits 0; the waiter exits 0, and its later trace line is `global lock: acquired after <n> ms (<k> retries)` with `n > 0`, after the waiting line; `config get check_interval_hours` gives 24.
   - every step: `assert_private_all`.

### Logging

- The E2E scenarios name every phase with `log.step` exactly as listed above, so a failure points at the phase. Each run's argv, overrides, exit, envelope and stderr events are recorded by `log.run`; each scenario also records the extracted trace lines per step with `log.json("trace lines", &lines)` and the `debug` lines with `log.json("debug lines", &lines)`. Scenario 1 hashes `<state>` and `<cache>` with `log.tree` before the warm steps and checks both with `log.assert_unchanged`, which logs the first differing paths. Scenario 3 records the spawned children's argv, pids, every stderr line in arrival order with its arrival time relative to the spawn, and the moment it resumed the holder, with `log.note` and `log.json`. On failure, the guard of T1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.1`, Structured test logs, and the `argc e2e` runner) prints `test log: <path>` and the last 20 steps.
- The contract rows log through the suite's `check()` context (`run.context()`: argv, exit, stdout and stderr) in every assertion message, and the snapshot diff names the row.
- Unit tests: each case name appears in its assertion message with the input (verbosity, level, quiet, mode, or the planted code line) and the output (the captured lines or the rendered text).

### Checkpoint-only tests

None new. The existing `status --cached` budget in `tests/perf.rs` (under 5 ms, median of 21, release build, ignored in the gate) covers the cost of the disabled trace calls; H6 runs it with `cargo test --release --test perf -- --ignored`.

## Considerations

- **Risks.** No milestone risk names this leaf. The implementation risks, and how to notice them:
  - *A level-1 output changes by accident* (a site rewritten to the wrong level, a field gated on `trace()`): commit 1's characterization snapshots, the 28 existing suites, and the source scan.
  - *A trace message leaks a private path or a credential:* privacy assertions on `WTF/`-planted homes in every E2E step, the kind-only rule for `local` and `url` refs, and `decision_line_never_names_a_local_or_url_ref`. Tokens never reach these sites: the memo stores public release ids, and the lock holder is a command name and a pid.
  - *The global sink deadlocks or slows a run:* `SINK` is released before the reporter is locked, worker threads never emit, and a disabled `emit` is one atomic load.
  - *clap changes its counting in an upgrade:* `a_repeated_v_counts_within_one_command_level` fails and names README's row.
- **Hot spots (§10.5) and how to share them.**
  - `src/cli.rs` (A1 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.1`, C1 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.3.1`, C2 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.3.2`, D5 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5` and E3 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.5.3` also edit it): this bead adds one statement in `run_with` and one test function, nothing in `Context`, `GlobalArgs` or the usage-fix code; rebase and keep them separate.
  - `src/output/stderr.rs`, `envelope.rs`, `mod.rs` (A2 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.2`, A3 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3` and E3 also edit them): whichever of A2 and this bead lands second puts `Trace` in `LogLevel::ALL` and `wire()`; A3's derives stay as they are.
  - `src/resolve/cache.rs` (D5 adds its `force_revalidate` choice): the plan's hot-spot table lists D5 alone for this file, but this bead edits it too. Its edits are confined to trace calls in `get()` and `probe()`, a timing in the probe closure, and the pure `decision_line`; whichever lands second rebases.
  - `src/fsx/lock.rs` (D4 `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.4` adds `Lease` and `LockUse::Expired`; the fsx rule is "E13 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.5.13`) first, G3 (`omad-7ccp`) last", with E3, D4 and B3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.3`) touching separate functions): this bead touches only `acquire_with_timeout` and its tests.
  - `README.md`: edit only the Global options row and the stderr events section.
- **Why size S, with no subtasks.** It is one invariant (three levels, level 1 unchanged, level 2 stderr-only) over small edits: two methods, one enum variant, a one-line gate, a 60-line module, 18 one-token replacements, three sites of a few lines each. The two commits of section 0 are an evidence order, not separate pieces of work.
- **Compatibility.** Older builds ignore `-vv` beyond `-v`. A consumer that switches on `level` with only `info` and `debug` sees a new value only when it asked for `-vv`. The widget reads no log events. Nothing persisted changes.
- **Performance.** Off, each site costs one atomic load and builds no string. On, the cost is the formatting and one locked write per line, which the user asked for.
- **Privacy.** See section 9 of the Technical Approach.

## Dependencies

Parent: AREA-A (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1`, the contract registry and the discovery surfaces).

**Blocked by:**
- T1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.1`, Structured test logs, and the `argc e2e` runner): `tests/e2e_verbosity.rs` uses `TestLog` (`tlog!()`, `log.run`, `log.tree`, `log.assert_unchanged`) and runs under `argc e2e`. The plan lists no blocker (this is one of its ten roots); the edge from T1 is added at filing because this bead writes integration tests itself and has no subtasks.

**Unblocks:**
- H1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.8.1`, The pre-freeze contract audit): the `trace` level is a wire shape, and every leaf that adds one lands before the audit, so the audit and H2's golden see `trace` among the `log` event's values.
- H4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.8.4`, The README final pass): it reconciles README, including the Global options row and the stderr events section this bead writes.
- T2 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.2`, Slice 1 end to end: self-describing (the demo, as a test)): it waits for every slice-1 leaf, this one included, so slice 1's demo runs on the finished slice (edge added at filing).

**Slice:** `slice-1`, "Self-describing". Its exit demo (run and recorded by T2): `capabilities --json` round-trips; `robot-docs schema` validates the whole matrix and every envelope snapshot, `details` included; the manifest's report prints; `robot-docs guide` equals `SKILL.md`, frontmatter first; `install-skill` into a throwaway `HOME`; `omaddons retail update` suggests `update -t retail`, `remove dbm retail` changes nothing, and the corpus runs; `completions bash` passes `bash -n`. It pre-checks checkpoint criteria 1, 2, 3 (part), 5 and 15. This bead adds no demo item; T2 only needs it closed.

**Related, not edges:** A2 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.2`) and A3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3`) for `LogLevel::ALL` and the event schemas; A5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.5`) for the schema snapshot; A10 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.10`) and H2 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.8.2`, The golden and the released-baseline mechanism) for the manifest; B1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.1`) for the guide; A1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.1`, Per-command facts in `COMMANDS`, and canonical names), C1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.3.1`, Misplaced clients before and after the verb), C2 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.3.2`, A client named as an addon, and `-t all`), D5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5`) and E3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.5.3`, `doctor diagnose` and `explain`) for `src/cli.rs`; D4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.4`, The plan store) for `src/fsx/lock.rs`. Lane guidance: the plan's six-lane schedule puts this bead in lane 6 at t = 6–7, after C2; it has 14 units of slack, so it never delays the critical path.

