description:
Part 5 of 5 of omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.3 (`robot-docs install-skill`). If this is the last open subtask of that bead, verify its acceptance criteria and close it as its body says.

## Background

B3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.3`) adds `omaddons robot-docs install-skill [--dir <DIR>]`, which writes the agent guide as `<DIR>/SKILL.md` (default `<skills>` = `$HOME/.claude/skills/omaddons`), byte-identical to `omaddons robot-docs guide` and the committed `skills/omaddons/SKILL.md` (M4-D7), refuses unsafe places and symlinks, keeps a locally edited copy as `SKILL.md.bak`, records a settings history line of kind `skill` with `dir`, keeps the folder in `history_tail.skill_dirs[]`, and offers other agents' skill roots as hints without writing there (M4-D8, M4-D50). Parts 1–4 built it with unit tests and the contract matrix rows.

**This part** proves the whole behaviour end to end through the real binary on synthetic homes, so a failure can be diagnosed from its log alone, and adds the real-machine test the checkpoint runs:
- `tests/robot_docs.rs::install_skill_*` (the plan's test plan: "default dir under `TestEnv`'s `HOME`, each refusal, unchanged, the history line, dry run"), extended to the edited copy, the hints, the lock, failure injection, `--if-match`, configuration independence, `status`, and the human output;
- `tests/common/skill.rs`, the helpers this suite, T2 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.2`, slice 1 end to end: "`install-skill` into a throwaway `HOME`"), B4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.4`, the recipes) and F10 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.6.10`, skill drift fixtures) share;
- `tests/real_machine.rs::install_skill_round_trip`, owned here and only run by H6 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.8.6`): §11.3 lists it among the three real-machine tests M4 adds (D7, E6 and B3 each own one), because M3's plan named real-machine tests nobody owned.

It serves checkpoint criterion 3 ("`install-skill` writes the same bytes to `<skills>/SKILL.md`, and a second run writes nothing") and criterion 17 ("the real-machine tests pass with every `SKIP` quoted"), and §3.3's decision: nothing in M4 installs into the real `$HOME/.claude/skills/` (a skill there is loaded by every Claude Code session on the machine, the owner's choice); the checkpoint proves the default path resolves (a dry run against the real home) and the install works (a real install into a scratch folder).

**Facts this part relies on** (as of `c0ab5e9`, plus T1 and parts 1–4):
- T1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.1`, structured test logs): `tests/common/tlog.rs` with `tlog!()`, `log.step`, `log.note`, `log.json`, `log.run(&runner, &argv) -> Ran` (`Ran::{ok, exit, envelope, data, error_code, warnings, commands, aborted, assert_private}`; runners: `TestEnv`, `common::home::Home`), `log.cmd(…)` for a run with extra env, cwd or failpoints, `log.tree`/`log.assert_unchanged` (tree hashes with modes and symlink targets; they refuse roots outside test directories), a panic guard printing `test log: <path>` and the last 20 steps, `OMADDONS_TEST_LOG=verbose`, and `argc e2e [FILTER]`, which runs every crate whose crate doc has a line starting `//! e2e suite:` (T1's convention test enforces "marker if and only if the crate uses `TestLog`").
- `TestEnv` (`tests/common/env.rs`): `home/`, `config/`, `state/`, `cache/`, `home/.local/share`, `TZ=UTC`, every other `OMADDONS_*` cleared; no `.claude` (`:51-55`). `common::home::Home::new(&["wow"])` builds a Battle.net root inside a Wine prefix (`tests/common/home.rs:27-53`); `common::trees::CustomRoot` builds a client outside any prefix (`tests/common/trees.rs:335-410`); clients hold `WTF/`, so common rule 9's privacy assertion applies; `common::trees::tree_hash` covers modes and symlink targets (`:437-475`).
- A held global lock in a test: `GlobalLock::acquire(&paths, "test")` in-process, then the binary times out after about 5 s with `locked` (exit 5, retryable, `fix_argv` the same argv) (`tests/targets.rs:392-413`).
- Failpoints (debug builds): `OMADDONS_FAILPOINTS=<name>[=abort|=error][@N]` (`src/fsx/failpoint.rs:3-12`); `fsx.write_atomic.before` (a `WriteFile`, `src/fsx/sys.rs:174`), `fsx.rename_with.before` (`:239`), `fsx.append_durable.before` (a history append, `:208`). An install-skill run's first `WriteFile` is `SKILL.md` itself: recovery with nothing pending writes nothing, directory creation is `fsx.create_dir`, the edited-copy move is a rename, the history line an append, and the projection and the doorbell are written after it.
- Real-machine conventions (`tests/real_machine.rs:1-75`): `checkpoint::require(test, MACHINE)` first (prints `SKIP <test>: OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE is not 1` and fails unless `OMADDONS_ALLOW_SKIP` names it, `tests/common/checkpoint.rs:13-41`); `support::omaddons(args) -> (code, envelope)` runs the real binary with `--json` and the real environment, failpoints and fixtures removed; `note(label, &value)` prints evidence with the home path as `<home>`; `forever_guard()` snapshots the Forever client (`:222-248`).

## Technical Approach

### 1. `tests/common/skill.rs` (and `pub mod skill;` in `tests/common/mod.rs`)

```rust
/// `skills/omaddons/SKILL.md` as committed (read from CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR): every
/// install must equal it byte for byte.
pub fn committed_guide() -> Vec<u8>;
/// Makes `<home>/.claude` (Claude Code set up, no skills yet); returns the default
/// skill folder `<home>/.claude/skills/omaddons` (not created).
pub fn claude_ready(env: &TestEnv) -> PathBuf;
/// Makes `<home>/<rel>` (".codex/skills", ".agents/skills", ".claude/skills"); returns it.
pub fn skill_root(env: &TestEnv, rel: &str) -> PathBuf;
/// Panics unless `file` holds exactly the committed guide, naming the first differing
/// line (both sides, at most 200 characters each) and both lengths.
pub fn assert_is_guide(file: &Path);
/// The committed guide with `edit` applied to its text and the stamp recomputed with
/// the library's stamp function (part 3's): another, pristine guide.
pub fn restamped_guide(edit: impl FnOnce(&mut String)) -> Vec<u8>;
/// `<cache>/omaddons/history_tail.json`'s `skill_dirs` as strings; `None` when the key
/// or the file is absent.
pub fn skill_dirs(env: &TestEnv) -> Option<Vec<String>>;
/// Every `kind: "skill"` line of `<state>/omaddons/history.jsonl`, parsed.
pub fn skill_lines(env: &TestEnv) -> Vec<serde_json::Value>;
```

The helpers read and create files in the test's own tempdir only; they never touch the developer's real `HOME`.

### 2. `tests/robot_docs.rs`: the end-to-end scenarios

The file (A5's) gains the crate-doc marker line `//! e2e suite: robot-docs schema, errors, guide and install-skill through the binary` if it does not have one, so `argc e2e robot_docs` runs it. Every scenario is a `TestLog` scenario (`let log = tlog!();`) on a fresh home; every command runs through `log.run` or `log.cmd`; every state check goes through `log.tree`/`log.assert_unchanged` or logs the values it compares with `log.json`. Paths below are relative to the home or to the `TestEnv` root; `<dir>` is the canonical skill folder the envelope reports.

1. **`install_skill_default_writes_the_guide_and_a_second_run_writes_nothing`**
   - seed: `skill_root(&env, ".claude/skills")`.
   - `robot-docs install-skill --json` → exit 0; `data` = `{dry_run: false, dir: <home>/.claude/skills/omaddons, file: <dir>/SKILL.md, written: "fresh", bytes: committed_guide().len(), tool_version: <envelope's tool_version>}`; `warnings` and `commands` empty.
   - check: `assert_is_guide(<dir>/SKILL.md)`; its mode is `0o644`; `robot-docs guide --json`'s `data.content` equals the file's bytes; `log.tree("skill dir", <dir>)`; `log.json("stat", {ino, mtime_ns})`.
   - again: the same command → exit 0, `written: "unchanged"`, same `bytes`; `log.assert_unchanged("skill dir", <dir>)`; inode and mtime equal; `skill_lines(&env).len() == 1`; `history.jsonl`'s length equal to after the first run.
2. **`install_skill_creates_skills_under_an_existing_claude_dir`**
   - seed: `claude_ready(&env)` and a planted `<home>/.claude/settings.json`.
   - run → `written: "fresh"`; `<home>/.claude/skills` and `<dir>` are directories whose permission bits equal those of a directory the test itself creates in the same tempdir with `std::fs::create_dir` (the same umask); `settings.json`'s bytes unchanged; `<home>/.claude` lists exactly `settings.json` and `skills`.
3. **`install_skill_without_claude_dir_is_not_found_and_offers_other_roots`**, three cases (`log.step` each):
   - `nothing`: `log.tree` over home, `<config>`, `<state>`, `<cache>`; run → exit 3, `error.code == "not_found"`, `details == {"path": "<home>/.claude"}`, `fix_argv == null`, `alternatives == []`, `retryable == false`; every tree unchanged; no `history.jsonl`.
   - `other_roots`: `skill_root(".codex/skills")`, `skill_root(".agents/skills")`; run → exit 3 with `alternatives` = the two argv `["omaddons","robot-docs","install-skill","--dir","<home>/.codex/skills/omaddons"]` then `.agents`; every tree unchanged; then the first alternative's argv, run as given → exit 0, `written: "fresh"`, `assert_is_guide`; `<home>/.claude` still absent.
   - `dry_run`: `--dry-run` without `.claude` → the same `not_found`.
4. **`install_skill_refuses_dirs_inside_clients_prefixes_and_its_own_dirs`**, on `Home::new(&["wow"])` plus a `CustomRoot` outside the prefix registered with `targets add <path> --name turtle` (exit 0). After setup, `log.tree` over home, both client dirs, `<config>`, `<state>`, `<cache>`. Cases, one `log.step` each, every run with `--progress json` and `Ran::assert_private` (`assert_private_all` over stdout and stderr):
   - `inside_registered_client`: `--dir <turtle>/Interface/omaddons` → exit 4, `scope_denied`, `details == {"reason":"skill_dir","path":<canonical>}`, message contains "inside the game client";
   - `client_dir_itself`: `--dir <turtle>` → the same refusal;
   - `inside_wine_prefix`: `--dir <prefix>/drive_c/omaddons` → "inside the Wine prefix";
   - `inside_config`, `inside_state`, `inside_cache`: `--dir <config>/omaddons/skill` (and the same under `<state>`, `<cache>`; the test creates each parent first) → "inside omaddons' own config folder" (`state`, `cache`);
   - `through_a_symlinked_ancestor`: `<home>/link -> <turtle>`, `--dir <home>/link/skills` → "inside the game client", `details.path` the resolved folder;
   - `missing_parent`: `--dir <home>/nope/omaddons` → exit 3, `not_found`, `details == {"path":"<home>/nope"}`;
   - `dir_is_a_file`: `--dir <home>/notes.txt` (a file) → exit 2, `usage`;
   - `non_utf8_dir`: an argv element with invalid UTF-8 bytes (built as an `OsString`; if `log.cmd` takes only strings, run it through `env.command()` and `log.json` the result) → exit 2, `usage`;
   - `relative_dir`: from the working directory `<home>/work`, `--dir skills/omaddons` → exit 0, `written: "fresh"`, `data.dir == <home>/work/skills/omaddons` (the one case that writes; its tree is excluded from the unchanged check).
   After every refusal: `log.assert_unchanged` over the setup trees, and `skill_lines` empty.
5. **`install_skill_refuses_a_symlinked_skill_md_and_leaves_it_untouched`**, with `<home>/.claude/skills/omaddons/` and `<home>/dotfiles/`. Cases: `link_to_other_bytes` (relative link to `dotfiles/omaddons.md`), `link_to_identical_copy` (the target holds `committed_guide()`), `dangling_link`, `absolute_link`. Each: `log.tree` of `<dir>` and `<home>/dotfiles`; run → exit 4, `scope_denied`, `details == {"reason":"symlink","path":"<dir>/SKILL.md","link_target":<the link text exactly>}`, the message contains "symlink"; both trees unchanged (the link's target recorded by the tree hash); no skill line; `--dry-run` gives the same error.
6. **`install_skill_records_a_skill_line_that_undo_steps_over`**, on `Home::new(&["wow"])` (a retail client) with a local archive built with `common::archives` (as `tests/contract/main.rs`'s `Scene::new` builds `foo.zip`):
   - `install gh:o/foo --file <zip> -t retail --json` → exit 0, tx `A`;
   - `claude_ready`; `robot-docs install-skill --actor agent --reason "test: skill line" --json` → `written: "fresh"`;
   - `history --json` → `entries[0]`: `kind: "skill"`, `dir == data.dir`, `target: null`, `actor: "agent"`, `reason: "test: skill line"`, the argv as run; `entries[1].tx == A`; no other entry has a `dir` key;
   - `history -t retail --json` → no skill entry;
   - `undo --dry-run --json` → selects `A`, not the skill line's tx;
   - `undo <the skill line's tx> --json` → exit 3, `not_found`;
   - `log.tree("skill dir", <dir>)`; `undo --json` → exit 0, reverts `A`; `log.assert_unchanged("skill dir", <dir>)`.
   Every run with `--progress json` and `Ran::assert_private`.
7. **`install_skill_keeps_skill_dirs_newest_first_and_bounded`**
   - ten parents `<home>/agents/a0` … `a9`; `install-skill --dir <home>/agents/aN/omaddons` for N = 0 … 9 → each `fresh`;
   - `skill_dirs(&env) == [a9, a8, …, a2]` (8 entries, canonical, `…/omaddons` each); `log.json("skill_dirs", …)`;
   - append a line to `a3`'s `SKILL.md`, rerun `--dir <a3>/omaddons` → `replaced` → `skill_dirs == [a3, a9, a8, a7, a6, a5, a4, a2]`;
   - delete `<cache>/omaddons/history_tail.json`; rerun `--dir <a3>/omaddons` (`unchanged`; `dispatch` rebuilds the missing projection) → the same list;
   - remove the `skill_dirs` key from the projection's JSON (test code); rerun the same command → the key is back with the same list.
8. **`install_skill_dry_run_writes_nothing_and_takes_no_lock`**
   - `claude_ready`; `log.tree` over home, `<config>`, `<state>`, `<cache>`.
   - `fresh`: `--dry-run --json` → `dry_run: true`, `written: "fresh"`; every tree unchanged; no `history.jsonl`.
   - install for real; `log.tree` again. `unchanged`: `--dry-run` → `written: "unchanged"`; trees unchanged.
   - edit `SKILL.md` (append a line); `log.tree`; `replaced`: `--dry-run --json` → `written: "replaced"`; `--dry-run` in human mode → stdout contains "would keep your edited copy as"; trees unchanged (no `.bak`).
   - lock: restore the guide's bytes; hold `GlobalLock::acquire(&paths, "test")`; `--dry-run` and a real (unchanged) run each exit 0 with `elapsed_ms` under 2,000 (they take no lock).
9. **`install_skill_replaces_an_outdated_guide_and_keeps_an_edited_copy`**, with `<home>/.claude/skills/omaddons/`. Cases:
   - `pristine_other_guide`: `SKILL.md` = `restamped_guide(|t| t.push_str("\nAn older paragraph.\n"))` → `written: "replaced"`; `assert_is_guide`; no `SKILL.md.bak`;
   - `edited_guide`: `committed_guide()` plus one appended line → `replaced`; `SKILL.md.bak` holds exactly the edited bytes; `assert_is_guide(SKILL.md)`;
   - `unstamped_file`: `# my notes\n` → `replaced`; `.bak` == `# my notes\n`;
   - `too_large_file`: 1 MiB + 1 bytes → `replaced`; `.bak` has the same length and SHA-256;
   - `older_bak_is_replaced`: an existing `.bak` with other bytes plus an edited `SKILL.md` → `.bak` now holds the newest edited copy.
   Each case appends exactly one skill line, and a second run is `unchanged`.
10. **`install_skill_offers_other_agent_roots_without_writing_there`**
    - `claude_ready`; `skill_root(".codex/skills")`, `skill_root(".agents/skills")`; `log.tree` of both roots.
    - default run → `commands` = two hints, `.codex` then `.agents`, each `{action: "install_skill", destructive: false, argv: […, "--dir", "<root>/omaddons"]}`; both roots unchanged.
    - run the first hint's `argv` as given → `fresh` into `<home>/.codex/skills/omaddons`.
    - default run again → `unchanged`, `commands` = the `.agents` hint only.
    - `--dir <home>/.codex/skills/omaddons` → `unchanged`, `commands` = the `.agents` hint only.
    - `<home>/.agents/skills` unchanged throughout.
11. **`install_skill_waits_for_the_global_lock_and_times_out_as_locked`**
    - `claude_ready`; hold the lock in-process; run → exit 5, `locked`, `retryable: true`, `fix_argv` = the argv run without presentation flags; elapsed ≥ 4 s; `SKILL.md` absent; no `history.jsonl`.
    - release; run → `fresh`.
12. **`install_skill_failures_leave_a_consistent_skill`**, with `<home>/.claude/skills/omaddons/`. Cases (each through `log.cmd(…).failpoints(…)`):
    - `write_fails_on_a_fresh_install`: `fsx.write_atomic.before@1=error` → exit 1, `io`; `SKILL.md` absent; no skill line; a plain run then succeeds (`fresh`), proving the lock was released;
    - `write_fails_after_the_edited_copy_moved`: an edited `SKILL.md`, the same failpoint → exit 1; `SKILL.md` absent; `.bak` equals the edited bytes; no new skill line; a plain run → `fresh`, `assert_is_guide`, `.bak` unchanged;
    - `history_line_fails`: `fsx.append_durable.before=error` → exit 0, `written: "fresh"`, `warnings` holds `history_not_recorded`; `assert_is_guide`; no skill line;
    - `crash_before_the_write`: `fsx.write_atomic.before@1=abort` → `Ran::aborted()`; `SKILL.md` as before the run (absent); no skill line; a plain run then takes the lock and succeeds.
13. **`install_skill_refuses_if_match`**: `claude_ready`; `robot-docs install-skill --if-match pc1:<64 zeros> --json` → exit 2, `usage`, `fix_argv == ["omaddons","help","robot-docs","install-skill"]`; the home tree unchanged.
14. **`install_skill_bytes_do_not_depend_on_config`**: `claude_ready`; a `<config>/omaddons/config.toml` setting `default_channel = "beta"`, `limits.snapshot_max_bytes`, `sources.wowi.enabled = false` and one `[[client_rules]]` override (each a documented key); install → `assert_is_guide`; `robot-docs guide --json`'s `data.content` equals `committed_guide()`. A failure is a defect in the guide's rendering (B1's): file it `discovered-from` this bead and block this bead on it.
15. **`status_never_recommends_install_skill`**: `claude_ready` (no skill installed): `status --json` and `status --cached --json` have no `commands[]` entry with action `install_skill`; after an install, the same.
16. **`install_skill_human_output`**: human mode (no `--json`), insta snapshots with the `TestEnv` root redacted as `<root>`: `fresh` with one `other agents:` line; `unchanged`; `replaced` keeping a copy; `--dry-run` `fresh`.

### 3. `tests/real_machine.rs::install_skill_round_trip`

```rust
#[test]
#[ignore = "real machine: OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE=1"]
fn install_skill_round_trip() {
    if !checkpoint::require("install_skill_round_trip", MACHINE) {
        return;
    }
    let forever = forever_guard();
    // …
    assert_eq!(forever_guard(), forever, "the Forever client never changes");
}
```

1. **Before:** the real `$HOME`; record `tree_hash` of `$HOME/.claude/skills/omaddons` (or "absent"), the length of `<state>/history.jsonl`, and the SHA-256 of `<cache>/history_tail.json` (or "absent"); `note` each.
2. **The dry run against the real home:** `omaddons(&["robot-docs", "install-skill", "--dry-run"])`, `note("install-skill --dry-run", …)`. If `$HOME/.claude` is a directory: exit 0, `data.dry_run: true`, `data.dir` is the canonical `$HOME/.claude/skills/omaddons`, `data.written` one of the three values. Otherwise: exit 3, `not_found`, `details.path` = `$HOME/.claude` (decided while writing this bead: both prove the default resolves). Then all three recorded values unchanged.
3. **The scratch install:** `scratch = std::env::temp_dir().join("omaddons-install-skill-round-trip")`, removed if a previous run left it, then created; assert that its canonical path is not under `$HOME/.claude/skills`, `$HOME/.codex/skills` or `$HOME/.agents/skills` (a scratch skill under a real root would be loaded by Claude Code while it exists). Decided while writing this bead: the path is fixed, not a random tempdir, so every checkpoint run names the same folder and `history_tail.skill_dirs[]` keeps one entry for all of them instead of filling its eight slots with deleted folders.
4. `omaddons(&["robot-docs", "install-skill", "--dir", <scratch>/omaddons, "--reason", "checkpoint: install_skill_round_trip"])` → exit 0, `written: "fresh"`; the file's bytes equal `omaddons(&["robot-docs", "guide"])`'s `data.content` and the repository's `skills/omaddons/SKILL.md` (from `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`).
5. The same command again → exit 0, `written: "unchanged"`; `history.jsonl`'s length unchanged by it.
6. **After:** remove the scratch folder; `$HOME/.claude/skills/omaddons`'s hash unchanged; `forever_guard()` unchanged.

The module doc gains one sentence: the test's one lasting effect is one `skill` settings line per run in the real history (never undone, like every settings line), naming the fixed scratch folder, which no longer exists afterwards (F10 does not report a deleted skill folder). §3.3's approval covers exactly this run.

### What not to do

- Never install into the real `$HOME/.claude/skills/` (or `.codex`, `.agents`) from any test.
- Never read or hash the developer's real `HOME` outside `install_skill_round_trip`; `TestLog` refuses such roots anyway.
- Never use a shell script or `rm -rf`; cleanup is Rust in the test.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `tests/common/skill.rs` provides `committed_guide`, `claude_ready`, `skill_root`, `assert_is_guide`, `restamped_guide`, `skill_dirs` and `skill_lines`, with their self-tests in `tests/common_selftest.rs`.
- [ ] `tests/robot_docs.rs` carries T1's end-to-end marker and the sixteen scenarios of §2 (fifteen `install_skill_*` and `status_never_recommends_install_skill`), each a `TestLog` scenario, all passing in the gate.
- [ ] The scenarios prove: the default install's bytes equal the committed guide and `robot-docs guide`; a second run writes nothing; `skills/` is created under an existing `$HOME/.claude`; no `$HOME/.claude` is `not_found` with runnable alternatives; every refusal of §2.4 and §2.5 changes nothing; the skill line is recorded and stepped over by `undo`; `skill_dirs[]` is newest first, bounded, rebuilt and repaired; `--dry-run` writes nothing and takes no lock; edited copies are kept; hints never write; the lock times out as `locked`; each injected failure leaves a consistent skill; `--if-match` is refused; the bytes do not depend on `config.toml`; `status` never recommends the skill.
- [ ] Scenarios built on `Home` run with `--progress json` and assert privacy over stdout and stderr.
- [ ] `tests/real_machine.rs::install_skill_round_trip` exists, is ignored and gated by `OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE` through `checkpoint::require`, never writes under a real skill root, guards the Forever client, and passes once on the development machine; its run (or its quoted `SKIP` line) is recorded in the close comment.
- [ ] `argc e2e robot_docs` runs the suite with verbose logs and prints the log root.
- [ ] `argc gate` passes; `ubs` is clean on the changed test files; `br lint` is clean for this subtask.

## Test Plan

### Unit tests

In `tests/common_selftest.rs` (helpers in `tests/common/` are compiled into every test crate, so their own tests live in the self-test crate):
- `restamped_guide_is_pristine_and_differs`: the result inspects as pristine (part 3's `inspect`) and its digest differs from `EXPECTED_DIGEST`.
- `assert_is_guide_names_the_first_differing_line`: a copy with line 7 changed panics with a message naming line 7 and both versions (`std::panic::catch_unwind`).
- `skill_dirs_reads_absent_and_present_keys`: a projection file without the key gives `None`; with it, the list.

### Integration and end-to-end tests

The sixteen scenarios of §2 in `tests/robot_docs.rs`, each with the steps and assertions given there, and the checkpoint-only test of §3.

### Logging

- Every scenario: `let log = tlog!();` then one `log.step` per phase named as in §2 (`seed`, `install`, `again`, a case's name), every command through `log.run`/`log.cmd` (argv, env overrides, failpoints, cwd, exit, envelope, stderr events, `net.log` lines), and every comparison either through `log.tree(label, root)` / `log.assert_unchanged(label, root)` (home, the skill folder, `<home>/dotfiles`, the other roots, client dirs, `<config>`, `<state>`, `<cache>`) or `log.json(label, &value)` before asserting (`skill_dirs`, the skill history lines, file stats, byte lengths and SHA-256s). A failure prints `test log: <path>` and the last 20 steps; `OMADDONS_TEST_LOG=verbose` (as `argc e2e robot_docs` sets it) echoes each step live.
- `assert_is_guide` and the byte comparisons print the first differing line and both lengths, never the whole guide.
- The real-machine test prints evidence with `note(label, &value)` (the home path shown as `<home>`): the before values, the dry run's envelope, both installs' envelopes and the after values. `TestLog` is not used there, since it refuses roots outside test directories by design.

### Checkpoint-only test

`tests/real_machine.rs::install_skill_round_trip`, run by H6 with `OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE=1 OMADDONS_LIVE=1 OMADDONS_ALLOW_SKIP=keyless_installs_forever cargo test --test real_machine -- --ignored --test-threads=1`, or alone with `OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE=1 cargo test --test real_machine install_skill_round_trip -- --ignored --test-threads=1`. Without `OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE=1` it prints `SKIP install_skill_round_trip: OMADDONS_REAL_MACHINE is not 1` and fails unless `OMADDONS_ALLOW_SKIP` names it; that skip is not pre-accepted (§3.2), so at the checkpoint it must run.

## Considerations

- **Duration:** scenario 11 waits about 5 s for the lock timeout (as `tests/targets.rs` does); everything else runs in milliseconds. Keep scenario 11 one case.
- **Failpoint counting** (scenario 12) depends on the write order part 4 fixed (`SKILL.md` is the first `WriteFile`). If part 4's order changes, the assertions (file absent, `.bak` intact) fail loudly rather than pass by accident.
- **A scenario that finds a defect elsewhere** (the renderer reading `config.toml`, the typo sweep demoting a fix) is filed as a bug `discovered-from` this bead and blocks it; the test is never weakened to pass.
- **T2 and F10** call `tests/common/skill.rs`; keep the helper names stable and documented.
- **Real machine:** the only test that reads the real home; it changes nothing there except one settings history line and the derived projection and doorbell, and it never touches a client (rule 10).

