## Background

B4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.4`) runs the eight recipes of the agent guide (`omaddons robot-docs guide`, the same bytes as `skills/omaddons/SKILL.md` and an installed skill, M4-D7) end to end, in the gate, on synthetic homes, so that the lines an agent copies are proven to work in at most two commands (checkpoint criterion 4). The plan fixes how: "run each on a fresh synthetic home with `tests/fixtures/http/skill_recipes/` (recorded once with `OMADDONS_RECORD=1` against the live hosts, then replayed)". Three of the recipes name real addons on real hosts (WeakAuras for Classic Era, GroupBulletinBoard's `main` for a 3.3.5a client, DBM for retail), and a fourth reinstalls them on a fresh machine; recorded answers are what make those recipes mean something.

**This part** builds that scenario and the homes everything runs on: `tests/common/recipes.rs` (the recipe home, the record plan, trimming and the hygiene check), `common::archives::skeleton`, the ignored recorder `record_skill_recipes`, the committed `tests/fixtures/http/skill_recipes/`, and the gate test that keeps it trimmed, public and small. It is its own step because it needs the network once and commits fixtures, which part 3's scenarios then only read; and part 4's live probe reuses its record plan.

**Facts this part relies on** (as of `c0ab5e9`, plus part 1 and the leaves before B4):
- Part 1 (omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.2.4.1): `common::guide::{recipes, recipe_argv, Recipe}` and `tests/skill_recipes.rs` (with the `//! e2e suite:` marker of T1, `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.1`, structured test logs, and the `CANONICAL` table).
- Debug builds replay `OMADDONS_HTTP_FIXTURES=<dir>` and, with `OMADDONS_RECORD=1`, record into it (`choose_transport`, `src/net/mod.rs:326-345`). Record mode forwards each request to the real network and writes `<dir>/<host>/<method>-<slug>-<hash>.json` (the `omaddons::net::replay::Fixture` format, one response) and a `.body` beside it, through fsx under the debug-only record-fixtures scope; it stores no request header, drops `set-cookie`, and strips secret query parameters from the URL and from `location` headers (`src/net/record.rs:1-110`). A second request for the same key overwrites the fixture.
- The recording transport is the innermost layer, under `Validating` (`src/net/mod.rs:316-321`). `Validating` keeps validators for feeds and file lists in `<cache>/http/` and sends `If-None-Match`/`If-Modified-Since` when it has one (`src/net/validators.rs:1-6`, `src/state/paths.rs:391-393`). **So a feed fetched twice in one recording home would record a `304` over its `200`**, and replay in a fresh home (no validator cache) would hand `Validating` a bare `304` and fail.
- Replay fails a load on two fixtures for one key or an unparsable file, and fails a request with no fixture as `internal` "replay: no fixture for <key>" (`src/net/replay.rs:108-195`).
- GitHub releases found through `releases/latest` and `git:` refs to GitHub carry no expected hash (`src/sources/github.rs:784`, `src/sources/git_github.rs:276`; the REST path for beta and alpha look-backs does, `src/sources/github_rest.rs:503`, and no recipe uses it), and `content-length` is read only to refuse an oversized response (`src/net/guard.rs:149-156`): a body replaced by a smaller archive replays and installs.
- The house recorders: `#[ignore = "records live fixtures: OMADDONS_RECORD=1"]`, an early return unless `OMADDONS_RECORD=1`, "Delete the directory first, then review the diff" (`tests/catalog.rs:69-90`, `tests/git_github.rs:53-90`); their Atom feeds are trimmed by hand to the newest entry with `<author><name>contributor</name></author>` (`tests/fixtures/http/git-github/github.com/get-fondlez-GroupBulletinBoard-commits-main.atom-118b95f0.body`).
- The committed fixtures total 2.6 MB, with one release archive (GroupBulletinBoard's 280 KB codeload zip).
- `Home::new(products)`, `Home::serve_recorded(name)`, `Home::std_command(args, extra)` (sets `OMADDONS_HTTP_FIXTURES` to `home.http` and `OMADDONS_PROC_ROOT`), `Home::seed_memo`, and the memo ageing in `Home::installed_behind` (`tests/common/home.rs:26-149, 254-266`); `CustomRoot::at(..).version(3, 3, 5, 12_340).build()` and `targets add <dir> --name wotlk` (`tests/git_github.rs:271-285`); `common::wtf::Wtf::at(client).saved_variables(folder, bytes).build()` with `FAKEACCT`/`FakeRealm`/`FakeChar` (`tests/common/wtf.rs:21-30, 54-69, 111`); `common::archives::zip_of` over the `zip` crate (`tests/common/archives.rs:1-30`); `flate2` is a dependency (`Cargo.toml`).
