## Technical Approach

### 1. `PlanBinding` (`src/app/precondition.rs`, beside `RemoveBinding`)

```rust
/// An engine command's run bound to its preview's token (M4-D19): its own plan's token,
/// witnesses and extras included, must be the preview's before anything is staged, and
/// its targets' generations must not have moved under the lock. D8 adds the under-lock
/// witness and operation checks to this type.
pub struct PlanBinding<'a> {
    command: &'static str,
    expected: Option<String>,
    extras: PlanExtras<'a>,
    preview: Vec<String>,
}

impl<'a> PlanBinding<'a> {
    pub fn new(command: &'static str, expected: Option<String>, extras: PlanExtras<'a>,
               preview: Vec<String>) -> Self { … }
    /// This run's binding: `Some` exactly when `--if-match` was given, dry run or not,
    /// with `preview_argv(&ctx.argv)` as the fix.
    pub fn of_run(ctx: &Context, command: &'static str, extras: PlanExtras<'a>) -> Option<Self> { … }
}

impl Binding for PlanBinding<'_> {
    fn plan(&self, plan: &Plan) -> Result<()> {
        let Some(expected) = &self.expected else { return Ok(()) };
        check(Some(expected), &of_plan(self.command, plan, &plan.witnesses, &self.extras), &self.preview)
    }
    fn undo(&self, _planned: &EngineUndo) -> Result<()> { Ok(()) }
    fn moved(&self, _target: &str) -> Error { stale(self.command, &[Part::Targets], &self.preview) }
}

/// A dry run's token: `of_plan` over the plan it ran, its witnesses and the extras.
pub fn plan_token(command: &'static str, plan: &Plan, extras: &PlanExtras<'_>) -> String

/// The witness scope of this run: `Some(WitnessScope::default())` for a dry run or a
/// bound run, `None` for an unbound real run (which compares nothing, so collects nothing).
pub fn witnessing(ctx: &Context) -> Option<WitnessScope>
```

- `expected: None` computes nothing and checks nothing, so D5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5`, `omaddons apply`) can construct one with the stored token, and the type has the plan's `PlanBinding { expected, extras }` shape.
- *Decided while writing this bead:* commands pass a binding only when `--if-match` is given (`of_run`); an unbound dry run computes its token afterwards with `plan_token` over `TxOutcomes.plan`, which is the same plan, witnesses and extras the binding would have seen. Unbound runs keep today's code path.
- `copy` builds its `WitnessScope` with a `CopyFrom` itself (subtask 4); `witnessing` is the default scope.

### 2. Bound dry runs check (`src/engine/tx.rs:401-407`)

Replace the match with:

```rust
let planned = plan::plan(&plan_req, &plan_ctx).and_then(|plan| match ctx.binding {
    // A bound run, dry or not, stages and reports nothing unless it planned what the
    // preview showed (M4-D19).
    Some(binding) => binding.plan(&plan).map(|()| plan),
    None => Ok(plan),
});
```

Nothing else in `tx.rs` changes. A refused bound dry run returns its `plan_stale` after cleanup exactly as a refused real run does (the existing `Err` branch at `:408-414` removes the planning scratch), so it writes nothing under `<state>` and never takes the global lock.

### 3. `remove` keeps its M3 dry run (`src/app/remove.rs:247-253`)

```rust
// A remove fetches nothing. `--if-match` binds the real run to its preview's plan; a
// dry run given a token previews afresh and returns the current one (M3-D46, kept).
let binding = ctx.if_match.clone().filter(|_| !ctx.dry_run).map(|token| precondition::RemoveBinding { … });
```

*Decided while writing this bead:* the plan says to drop the engine's condition; done alone, that turns `remove --dry-run --if-match <stale>` into `plan_stale`, against criterion 6 ("the M3 binding of `remove` … is unchanged"), the M3 test and README. `undo`, `backup restore`, `backup prune` and `errors dismiss` never reach `tx::run`'s plan seam and are untouched. How `apply --dry-run` reports a stale stored M3 plan is D5's decision.

### 4. `check_noop` and `Plan::idle`

```rust
// src/engine/plan.rs, beside `Plan::has_ops`
/// The plan of a run that changes nothing on `targets`, each with the record generation
/// it was judged at: one empty `TargetPlan` per target (no ops, changes, releases,
/// warnings or work; `creates_addons_dir: false`), no failures, no witnesses.
pub fn idle(targets: &[(&Target, u64)], argv: &[String], actor: Actor) -> Plan

// src/app/precondition.rs
/// One in-scope target of a run that found nothing to change.
pub struct Idle<'a> { pub target: &'a Target, pub generation: u64 }

/// The token of a run that changes nothing on `targets`: `of_plan` over `Plan::idle`,
/// each target witnessed with `witness::bare` (marker and judge), plus `extras`.
pub fn of_noop(command: &'static str, targets: &[Idle<'_>], extras: &PlanExtras<'_>) -> Result<Precondition>

/// The check of a no-op path, one line at each call site:
/// - an unbound real run: `Ok(None)`, computing and reading nothing;
/// - otherwise: `of_noop`, then `check(ctx.if_match, …, preview_argv(&ctx.argv))`
///   (`plan_stale` when it differs), then `Ok(Some(token))` for a dry run, `Ok(None)`
///   for a bound real run that matched.
pub fn check_noop(ctx: &Context, command: &'static str, targets: &[Idle<'_>], extras: &PlanExtras<'_>) -> Result<Option<String>>
```

- `of_noop` goes through `of_plan` so its canonical form is exactly an engine token's: a preview with work and a bound run with none (or the reverse) differ in `selection`, and a preview with nothing to do and an unchanged bound run with nothing to do agree.
- Fields of the idle plan the token does not read (`created_at`, `argv`, `actor`, `default_kind`) take the given or default values; `generations` maps each target's key or provisional id to its generation, as `plan::plan` does.
- `witness::bare` failing (an unreadable marker) fails `of_noop` with D1's `io` error: fail closed (§8.1 rule 6).
- This subtask adds the helpers only; subtasks 3 and 4 call `check_noop` at `update.rs:312`, `sync.rs:673` and `copy.rs:288`, before `recover_waiting`, with their in-scope targets and extras.

