description:
Part 3 of 7 of omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5 (`omaddons apply`). If this is the last open subtask of that bead, verify its acceptance criteria and close it as its body says.

## Background

D5 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5`) adds `omaddons apply <plan_id>`, which executes a stored plan exactly as previewed. A stored plan (D4, `omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.4`, the plan store) holds a `StoredIntent`: a typed, versioned enum with one variant per storable command (`install`, `update`, `pin`, `unpin`, `adopt`, `sync`, `copy`, `remove`, `undo`, `backup restore`, `backup prune`), each holding that command's normalized arguments (absolute paths, resolved target keys, typed safety options). `apply` must turn that intent back into the command's own argument struct, call the command's own `run`, and wrap the typed outcome it gets back, without ever re-parsing an argv.

This subtask builds that typed machinery, with no command surface yet:

- `StoredIntent::execute(&ctx) -> Result<StorableOutcome>` and the eleven `From<&XIntent> for XArgs` conversions;
- `StorableOutcome`, one variant per storable command, with `target_outcomes()` (M4-D61's per-target report);
- `ApplyData`, the wrapper union whose schema is one complete variant per storable command;
- `app::emit_side_events`, the one helper the dispatch arms and `apply` use for the debug notes and `lock_released` events (M4-D23 "one render").

It is its own step because it is pure types and conversions, testable without the command, touching `src/app/intent.rs`, `src/app/apply.rs` (new) and `src/app/mod.rs`'s arms; it can start at once, in parallel with subtask 1 (omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5.1). Subtask 4 (omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.4.5.4) builds the context it executes in and the command around it.

**M4-D23, restated (what this subtask implements):** `StoredIntent::execute(&ctx)` builds the command's own argument struct from the intent and calls the command's `run` directly; each storable `run` already returns a typed outcome, so `apply` receives a `StorableOutcome` before anything renders. No argv is re-parsed, and an intent can never name `apply`, `doctor`, `auth` or any other non-storable command, because the enum has no such variant. One render: a direct invocation renders its outcome; `apply` wraps it and renders once; the debug notes and `lock_released` events the dispatch arms emit move into one shared helper that both use; no capturing output adapter exists. `data` is `ApplyData {plan_id, applied: {command, display_argv}, approved?, result, outcomes[]}`, its schema "a union of complete wrapper variants, generated from a serde enum with one variant per storable command. Each variant fixes `applied.command` with `const` and gives `result` that command's data schema; `approved` is the shared `Approval` schema. A union on `result` alone would not tie it to its sibling `applied.command`, so the contract suite rejects a mismatched command/result pair and an unknown nested result field." *Rejected:* re-dispatching a stored argv through `Cli::try_parse_from` with a capturing output adapter (the parser became a storage format, and decoding proved nothing about whether command, argv, parts and token agreed).

**M4-D61, restated (the report):** each target is reported as `committed`, `unchanged`, `stale` or `failed`, with its transaction id or error code, one `{target, key, status, tx, error_code}` per target, in target order. Nothing calls a multi-target run atomic.

**Facts this subtask relies on** (verified at `c0ab5e9`):
- The storable `run` functions and their outcomes: `install::run` → `InstallOutcome` (data `InstallData`, `src/app/install.rs:95-112, 206-222, 402`); `update::run` → `UpdateOutcome` (`TargetsData`; `src/app/update.rs:40-71, 127`); `pin::pin`/`pin::unpin` → `PinOutcome` (`TargetsData`; `src/app/pin.rs:76-85, 113, 124`); `adopt::run` → `AdoptOutcome` (`AdoptData`, untagged `Report(AdoptReport) | Adopted(TargetsData)`; `src/app/adopt.rs:58-85, 188-204, 467`); `sync::run` → `SyncOutcome` (`src/app/sync.rs:65-75, 614`); `copy::run` → `CopyOutcome` (`src/app/copy.rs:59-71, 167`); `remove::run` → `RemoveOutcome` (`RemoveData`, `src/app/remove.rs:44-56, 82-91, 164`); `undo::run` → `UndoOutcome` (`UndoData` with `transactions: Vec<UndoTx {target, reverted, tx, status, error}>`, `src/app/undo.rs:61-143, 167-178, 333`); `backup::restore_backup` → `BackupRestoreOutcome` (`BackupRestoreData`, `src/app/backup.rs:1564-1600, 1641-1656, 1826`); `backup::prune_backups` → `BackupPruneOutcome` (`BackupPruneData {dry_run, targets: [BackupPruneTarget {target, pruned, busy, kept, reclaimed_for_space, error}], precondition}`, `src/app/backup.rs:2173-2214, 2285`). Every data type derives `Debug, Clone, Serialize, JsonSchema`.
- `TargetsData` (`src/app/outcome.rs:246-256`) is `{dry_run, run, targets: [TargetResult {target: TargetRef {id, key, mode?}, tx, kind, no_section, items, reload_required, atomic_swap, creates_addons_dir, error: Option<ErrorBody>}], summary}`, sorted by target id; `ItemResult.status` is `ItemStatus` (`installed`, …, `unchanged`, `skipped`, `failed`) with `error: Option<ItemError {code, …}>` (`:52-126, 166-181, 277-302`).
- The arms' side events (`src/app/mod.rs:374-587`): install logs `notes` then `lock_released(lock_held_ms, data.tx)`; update, sync, copy, adopt and `out_pin` (`:317-327`) log `notes` then each `(tx, ms)` of `locks`; undo logs each lock; remove and backup restore log `lock_released(lock_held_ms, data.tx)`; info, export, outdated, search and errors log `notes`; status logs a discovery line, then its notes; backup prune logs nothing. `Out::log` and `Out::lock_released` are private to `src/app/mod.rs` (`:302-313`).
- The `Outcome` trait (`src/output/mod.rs:34-55`): `command`, `data`, `warnings`, `commands`, `partial`, `assertion_failure`, `render_human`. An `Ok` outcome with `partial: true` exits 0; `assertion_failure` turns it into exit 6 with the data kept.
- `--strict` exists on `install`, `update`, `sync` and `copy` (`src/app/{install,update,sync,copy}.rs`, `pub strict: bool`): exit 6 when only some items succeed.
- A hand-written `JsonSchema` has precedent (`Error` delegates to `ErrorBody`, `src/error.rs:645-653`; ULID ids, `src/model.rs:265-276`).
- A3 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.1.3`, schemas)'s strict transform and composition tests model `apply`'s schema as a `oneOf` whose variants carry `applied.command` as a `const` and a `result` `$ref` (`one_of_with_shared_fields`); A3 refuses `anyOf` for unions (it would admit an object matching two variants' fields). schemars emits `anyOf` for an untagged enum.

## Technical Approach

### 1. One table, three generated types

In `src/app/apply.rs` (new), a declarative macro with one row per storable command, in the plan's order:

```rust
storable_commands! {
    // variant,      path,             intent,         args,               run,                     outcome,               data
    Install,       "install",        InstallIntent,  InstallArgs,        install::run,            InstallOutcome,        InstallData;
    Update,        "update",         UpdateIntent,   UpdateArgs,         update::run,             UpdateOutcome,         TargetsData;
    Pin,           "pin",            PinIntent,      PinArgs,            pin::pin,                PinOutcome,            TargetsData;
    Unpin,         "unpin",          PinIntent,      UnpinArgs,          pin::unpin,              PinOutcome,            TargetsData;
    Adopt,         "adopt",          AdoptIntent,    AdoptArgs,          adopt::run,              AdoptOutcome,          AdoptData;
    Sync,          "sync",           SyncIntent,     SyncArgs,           sync::run,               SyncOutcome,           TargetsData;
    Copy,          "copy",           CopyIntent,     CopyArgs,           copy::run,               CopyOutcome,           TargetsData;
    Remove,        "remove",         RemoveIntent,   RemoveArgs,         remove::run,             RemoveOutcome,         RemoveData;
    Undo,          "undo",           UndoIntent,     UndoArgs,           undo::run,               UndoOutcome,           UndoData;
    BackupRestore, "backup restore", RestoreIntent,  BackupRestoreArgs,  backup::restore_backup,  BackupRestoreOutcome,  BackupRestoreData;
    BackupPrune,   "backup prune",   PruneIntent,    BackupPruneArgs,    backup::prune_backups,   BackupPruneOutcome,    BackupPruneData;
}
```

(The intent type names are D4's; use its actual names.) It generates:

- `pub enum StorableOutcome { Install(InstallOutcome), … }`;
- `impl StoredIntent { pub fn execute(&self, ctx: &Context) -> Result<StorableOutcome> }`: `Self::Install(i) => install::run(ctx, &InstallArgs::from(i)).map(StorableOutcome::Install)`, …;
- `mod tag { pub enum Install { Install } … }`, each serialized as its path (`#[serde(rename = "install")]`, `"backup restore"`);
- `pub enum ApplyData { Install(Wrapper<tag::Install, InstallData>), … }` and its `JsonSchema` (section 4);
- `pub const STORABLE_PATHS: &[&str]` in row order.

A unit test asserts `STORABLE_PATHS` equals the `COMMANDS` rows with `stores_plan: true` (D4 sets them) and the `StoredIntent` variants' paths, in the same order, so a twelfth storable command cannot be added in one place only. A macro is not a script changing code: it is source, reviewed like any other.

### 2. The conversions (`src/app/intent.rs`)

`impl From<&InstallIntent> for InstallArgs` and the ten others, beside D4's `StoredIntent::from_args` (their inverse):

- **Total over the Args fields.** Each conversion builds the Args with every field named. A field the intent carries comes from the intent (the refs as their normalized strings, an absolute `file`, the channel's wire name, `reinstall`, `force`, `no_deps`, an undo's resolved transaction ids, a backup id, …). A field the intent does not carry takes its clap default, and the doc comment of the conversion lists each such field and why: `strict: false` (it changes only the exit code of a partial result; `apply` reports partial results through `partial` and `outcomes[]`, so `apply`'s `COMMANDS` row declares no exit 6, A1's rule tying 6 to a command's own `--check`/`--strict`); `refresh: false` (`apply` forces revalidation; `Refresh` would win only if an intent carried it). If D4's intent carries `strict`, the conversion still sets `false` and the close comment says so.
- **Not Args fields:** the target selector and `--while-running` are `Context` fields (`-t` and `--while-running` are global flags). Subtask 4's derived context sets them from the intent; the conversion ignores them.
- **Accessors** subtask 4 needs, added here to `StoredIntent` if D4 did not: `command(&self) -> &'static str` (the path, from the macro's table), `target_selector(&self) -> Option<String>` (the resolved key, or provisional id; `None` when the intent covers every target), `while_running(&self) -> bool`, `inputs(&self) -> Vec<&AbsPath>` (every absolute local input: an install's `--file` archive or directory, a `file:` ref's path, a `sync` file).

### 3. `StorableOutcome`

- `impl StorableOutcome`: `command() -> &'static str`; `warnings()`, `commands()`, `partial()`, `assertion_failure()`, `render_human(w, style)` forwarded to the inner outcome (through `output::Outcome`); `precondition() -> Option<&str>` (the data's token field: `InstallData.precondition`, `TargetsData.precondition` (D2, D3), `AdoptData::Adopted(..).precondition`, `RemoveData.precondition`, `UndoData.precondition`, `BackupRestoreData.precondition`, `BackupPruneData.precondition`; `None` for `AdoptData::Report`); `target_outcomes() -> Vec<TargetOutcome>` (section 5); `into_data(self)` or a borrowing builder for `ApplyData` (section 4).
- **Side events:** `impl SideEvents for StorableOutcome` delegates to the inner outcome (section 6).

### 4. `ApplyData` and its schema

```rust
/// One storable command's `apply` data.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, JsonSchema)]
pub struct Wrapper<C, D> {
    pub plan_id: PlanId,
    pub applied: Applied<C>,
    /// `--dry-run`: the approval stored with the plan (M4-D24); `null` on a real run.
    pub approved: Option<Approval>,
    /// The executed command's own data.
    pub result: D,
    /// One per target of the result, sorted by target id (M4-D61).
    pub outcomes: Vec<TargetOutcome>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, JsonSchema)]
pub struct Applied<C> {
    /// The executed command's canonical path, as `COMMANDS` and the envelope name it.
    pub command: C,
    /// The argv a person would type for the plan's intent; documentation, never parsed.
    pub display_argv: Vec<String>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
#[serde(untagged)]
pub enum ApplyData { Install(Wrapper<tag::Install, InstallData>), /* … one per row */ }
```

