    pub error_code: Option<ErrorCode>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, JsonSchema)]
#[serde(rename_all = "snake_case")]
pub enum OutcomeStatus { Committed, Unchanged, Stale, Failed }
```

`target_outcomes()`, sorted by target id:

| Data | One entry per | `committed` | `stale` | `failed` | `unchanged` |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `TargetsData`, `AdoptData::Adopted` | `targets[]` | `tx` set | no tx, `error.code == plan_stale` | no tx and another `error`, or no tx and an item `failed` (`error_code` the first failed item's) | no tx, no error, no failed item |
| `InstallData`, `RemoveData` | the one target | `tx` set | no tx and the first failed item's code is `plan_stale` | no tx and an item failed (its code) | otherwise |
| `UndoData` | each distinct `transactions[].target`, by id | an undone transaction on it (`tx` the last undo tx there) | no undo on it, its first error `plan_stale` | no undo on it, another error | — |
| `BackupRestoreData` | the one target | `tx` set | — | — | no tx |
| `BackupPruneData` | `targets[]` | `pruned` non-empty (`tx: null`: a prune writes no transaction or history line) | `error.code == plan_stale` | another `error` | nothing pruned, no error |
| `AdoptData::Report` | — | — | — | — | no entries (report mode stores no plan) |

- A dry run commits nothing: every entry without an error is `unchanged` with `tx: null`; `result` says what would change. Decided while writing this bead: this meaning keeps the plan's closed set of four.
- `target` is `TargetRef.id`; `key` is `TargetRef.key`.

### 6. `app::emit_side_events` (`src/app/mod.rs`)

```rust
/// What a dispatch arm logs about an outcome before rendering it: its `-v` debug notes,
/// then one `lock released` line per transaction the run committed.
pub(crate) trait SideEvents {
    fn notes(&self) -> &[String] { &[] }
    fn locks(&self) -> Vec<(TxId, u64)> { Vec::new() }
}

fn emit_side_events(out: &Out<'_>, events: &dyn SideEvents) {
    for note in events.notes() { out.log(output::LogLevel::Debug, note); }
    for (tx, ms) in events.locks() { out.lock_released(Some(ms), Some(tx)); }
}
```

- Implementations: `InstallOutcome` (`notes`; `locks` = `(data.tx, lock_held_ms)` when both are set), `UpdateOutcome`, `PinOutcome`, `SyncOutcome`, `CopyOutcome`, `AdoptOutcome` (`notes`, `locks`), `UndoOutcome` (`locks`), `RemoveOutcome` and `BackupRestoreOutcome` (`(data.tx, lock_held_ms)`), `BackupPruneOutcome` (nothing), and the read commands that log notes (`InfoOutcome`, `ExportOutcome`, `OutdatedOutcome`, `SearchOutcome`, `ErrorsOutcome`). `StorableOutcome` delegates; subtask 4's `ApplyOutcome` returns its own notes followed by the executed outcome's.
- Every arm that logs only these calls `emit_side_events(out, &outcome)` on `Ok` (`out_pin` is removed); `status` keeps its discovery line and then calls it for its notes. The order of lines is exactly today's, so stderr is byte-identical for every direct invocation (the existing `-v` and NDJSON tests are the proof).

