## Background

**What this is.** Three kinds of error still tell the user to run a command that cannot help, because they were written before the doctor existed. An `internal` error (a bug or a panic) says `omaddons status`. A state file omaddons cannot read says `omaddons status`. A journal that recovery leaves "for manual repair" says to read a README section, or to run `omaddons status`, which shows the same journal and offers no way out. This bead points each of them at the doctor: an internal error at `omaddons doctor` (never at the command that just failed), an unreadable state file at the doctor's explanation of `fm-schemas-state-corrupt`, and each stuck journal at the doctor's explanation of exactly its state, `omaddons doctor explain <fm> -t <id>`. It changes no recovery behaviour, adds no error code, no `details` key and no command: it changes which command a fix names, and proves that every fix it names runs.

It is the second half of M4-D53 (F8 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.6.8`, `status` on the registry) is the first: `auto_fixable`, `explain` and the doctor-fix remediations on `status`'s issues), and the last of the handoffs earlier milestones addressed to M4 that touch fixes (M4-D1: "the `internal` and `state_corrupt` fixes pointing at the doctor (DEC-5, `error.rs:360-363`, `store.rs:404-407`)").

