## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `internal_fix()` is `omaddons doctor`. `internal_fix_for` gives `status` → `omaddons status --cached`; `status --cached` → the bug-report prose (no argv); `doctor health` → the bug-report prose; every other `doctor` path → `omaddons doctor health`; every other command, and a panic before the command is known, → `omaddons doctor`.
- [ ] No fix reruns the failing command for an internal error: from every `app::COMMANDS` path, following the internal fix reaches a prose fix in at most three hops and never repeats an argv (unit test), and the same holds end to end with the panic failpoint armed at every hop.
- [ ] Every production `internal` error is built by `Error::internal` or is a recovery stop (source scan); `src/net/replay.rs`'s "no fixture" error is one of them.
- [ ] A state file that does not read or decode (`state_corrupt`, and `io` for a read failure) carries `fix_argv` `["omaddons","doctor","explain","fm-schemas-state-corrupt"]`; a newer state file still carries `upgrade omaddons`.
- [ ] Each recovery stop error carries `omaddons doctor explain <fm> -t <id>` with the failure mode of its `details.reason` (`journal_too_new`, `journal_unreadable`, `marker_mismatch`, `step_unrecognized`, `unexpected_state`, `preservation_incomplete`) and the target's registry id; without a registry entry for the target, no `-t`; `unattributed` points at `fm-concurrency_primitives-journal-unattributed` without `-t`, or at `fm-schemas-state-corrupt` when it names no journal. Code, message and `details` are unchanged.
- [ ] The `journal_pending` warnings that report a stop (another client's stop during a commit, a reader's unrecoverable journal, `recover_under`'s unrecoverable failure) carry the same fix as the error; `recovery_failed` carries the recovery error's fix when that error is a stop.
- [ ] Unchanged: the game wait's prose (`saved_variables`), the recoverable journal's `omaddons status` warning, `journal_recovered`'s fix, recovery's `io` errors, and `recovery_failed` for an I/O failure.
- [ ] **Every fix still parses and runs.** Each new fix argv, run on the home that produced it (the failpoint disarmed), exits as its command documents: `doctor explain` 0 with the stuck journal's instance in `instances[]` (or the corrupt file's), `doctor` and `doctor health` 0 on a clean home, `status --cached` 0; never 64 or 74. `doctor explain` writes nothing (tree hashes of `<state>`, `<cache>`, `<config>` and every client dir unchanged). The contract checks pass on every new row, and `tests/contract/intent_corpus.rs` passes unchanged where C4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.3.4`) has landed.
- [ ] Recovery's behaviour is unchanged: `tests/engine_crash.rs`, `tests/journal.rs` and E11's differential test pass, with only fix assertions edited.
- [ ] Every test that pinned an old fix (Technical Approach §6) asserts the new one; §6's grep finds no stale pin.
- [ ] Contract rows (`tests/contract/matrix.rs`) for an internal error, a stuck journal and a corrupt registry are snapshotted; `a_panic_is_one_internal_envelope` in `tests/contract/special.rs` covers the doctor tree (exit 74, `doctor health`).
- [ ] Where A5 has landed, the six fix patterns of §7 are rewritten and pass A5's style and command-path tests; generated-listing snapshots are re-accepted with only those rows changed; where B1 has landed, `skills/omaddons/SKILL.md` is regenerated and `cargo test --test skill` passes.
- [ ] README's panic paragraph, the `internal`, `state_corrupt`, `io`, `state_too_new` and `scope_denied` rows, the `journal_pending` warning row and the Troubleshooting entry describe the new fixes, in the same commit.
- [ ] No output names an account, realm or character: `assert_private_all` over stdout and stderr, with `--progress json`, in every scenario that plants a `WTF/` journal.
- [ ] `argc gate` passes and `ubs` is clean on the changed files.
- [ ] The close comment lists every changed fix (code or warning, site, before → after) with a compatibility note (no wire name added, renamed or removed; a fix's argv is a value agents run), the final fix-pattern texts, that no mutating command path was added or changed (common rule 16; M4-D22 not needed), that no constant was added, and every "Decided while writing this bead" item confirmed or adjusted.
