### Logging

- Every scenario of `tests/doctor_fixes.rs` opens `let log = tlog!();` and names its phases with `log.step(…)`: "home", "plant <case>", "fail", "check journal set", "run the fix", "check trees", "other client". Every command goes through `log.run(&env, &argv)`, so its argv, environment overrides (`OMADDONS_FAILPOINTS`, `OMADDONS_PROC_ROOT`), exit, envelope, stderr events and `net.log` lines are in `steps.jsonl` and `transcript.md`.
