## Background

F9 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.6.9`) is the doctor's safety harness: `tests/doctor_harness.rs` and `tests/doctor/`, run in every gate, which put every real failure mode's fixture and every real fixer through fourteen properties (round trip through `doctor undo`, idempotence, a real crash at every primitive boundary, concurrency, repeatability, true positive, no false positive, purity, coverage, blast radius, verbatim backups, cross-failure-mode pairs, the lock file, status agreement). It exists because each doctor leaf proves only its own part on its own cases, and the plan deliberately left every undo round trip of the real fixers to one leaf blocked by E7 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.5.7`, the generic undo of repairs) and by every fixer (M4-D47: fixtures are Rust, in `tests/doctor/`, and coverage is bidirectional; rejected: shell `corrupt.sh`/`assert.sh`). It serves §3.2 criterion 9 and G-M4-4 ("every auto-fixable state … is proven by a fixture that round-trips").

**This part** builds the runner every property stands on, and nothing that asserts a property: lanes (each fixture's corrupted home built once and restored per case, which is how the harness meets its 60 s target without dropping a crash position), subject maps and the bookkeeping rule, the doctor-run helpers and typed report views, the capabilities view, the case pool, and four additive methods on the `Fixture` trait. It ends with self-tests of the runner and with the fidelity test over every fixture, which decides which fixtures cannot be copied. It is its own step because parts 2 to 5 all build on it and can then run in parallel.

