## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `tests/doctor_harness.rs` exists, debug-only, with its `//! e2e suite:` line, and includes the fixtures and `tests/doctor/harness/` by path; `argc e2e doctor_harness` runs it.
- [ ] The `Fixture` trait has the four defaulted methods `name`, `finds`, `evidence_keys` and `copy_safe`, each documented, and every existing suite that includes the fixtures compiles and passes unchanged.
- [ ] `Lane::build`, `restore` (in place, preserving bytes, modes, symlink targets and mtimes) and `fidelity` work as specified; `a_restored_lane_equals_its_template` passes.
- [ ] `SubjectMap`, `Bookkeeping` (exclusions keyed by the run's own ids, never by directory name) and `root_map` work as specified; `subject_maps_compare_content_and_name_differences` passes, including the subject-rule panic.
- [ ] The doctor-run helpers, typed reports, `caps` (from `doctor capabilities` once E4 has landed, else built from the registry and the scope roots) and `assert_blast_radius` exist; `blast_radius_flags_a_write_outside_the_declared_scopes` passes.
- [ ] The pool shares one slot budget across the binary and reports every failing case; `the_pool_runs_every_case_and_reports_every_failure` passes.
- [ ] `every_fixture_survives_a_copy_or_says_so` passes, the lock-held-long control fails fidelity as expected, and each fixture whose `copy_safe()` became `false` says why in a comment and in the close comment.
- [ ] `argc gate` passes; `ubs` is clean on the changed files.

## Test Plan

### Unit tests

None in `src/`. The runner's helpers need homes and the binary, so they are tested by the self-tests below.

### Integration and end-to-end tests

The five self-tests of Technical Approach item 7, in `tests/doctor/harness/props/selftest.rs`, compiled into `tests/doctor_harness.rs`. The fidelity test runs `doctor --json` with each fixture's selection (part of `run::diagnose`) twice per fixture.

### Logging

- Each self-test opens `let log = tlog!();`. `a_restored_lane_equals_its_template` logs steps "plant", "save", "modify", "restore", "compare", "clear", with `log.json("template entries", …)` and, on a mismatch, the first differing entries (T1's `tree_diff`).
- The subject-map test logs one `log.case(<row>)` per table row with both maps (`log.json("before", …)`, `log.json("after", …)`) and the `same_content` result.
- The fidelity test logs one `log.case(<fixture name>)` per fixture with steps "build", "diagnose original", "restore", "diagnose copy", "compare", the two `findings` arrays (`log.json`), the build and restore times, and the result; the control case says it expects `Err`.
