## Background

**The leaf.** T4 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.4`) turns the exit demo of M4's slice 3, "Diagnose and repair", into a suite in the gate, `tests/e2e_slice3.rs`, and records the demo on the milestone epic (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm`) as "**Slice demo 3. Diagnose and repair**". The demo, as the plan's §10.6 states it: "`doctor` on a home with each §2.3 stuck state planted; a set-aside with `--force --yes`, then `doctor undo`; a set-aside, a later install, and the refused undo; a stuck repair that fences only its own resources; a bound gc; the credential fix from the Issues view (QML) and Undo last; the harness green at every primitive boundary; the fsync counts table". M3 recorded its slice demos only at the end of the milestone; M4 makes each demo a test that runs in every gate once its slice has landed. The suite owns no feature code and adds no wire name: it drives the real binary on synthetic homes through the helpers the slice's leaves wrote (M4-D47: fixtures and helpers are Rust, never shell scripts), and a demo item that fails is a defect in the leaf that owns the behaviour, fixed there and filed `discovered-from` omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.9.4.

**This part** creates the suite and its first demo item. It is its own step because everything later in the leaf builds on the crate root and the support module, and because item 1 is the heaviest scenario: the eight stuck journal states of checkpoint criterion 11 planted together on one home, each named alike by `status` and `doctor`. Criterion 11, restated: every manual-repair state (`journal_too_new`, `journal_unreadable`, marker mismatch, a step in neither state, `unexpected_state`, `preservation_incomplete`, a journal with no readable target, and a restore journal waiting for the game) has a finding with a correct title in both `status` and `doctor`. Criterion 12: `status`'s issues come from the registry's `cached` and `quick` tiers, and the issue ids it reports equal the doctor's findings of those tiers. Criterion 9 (part): bare `doctor` changes nothing outside `<state>/doctor/`, checked by tree hashes of `<state>`, `<cache>`, `<config>` and every client dir, and detectors are repeatable. Criterion 10 (part): `doctor health` prints one line whose first token is `ok`, `findings`, `unsafe` or `concurrency`.

Decided while writing this bead: "each §2.3 stuck state" is read as criterion 11's eight states, which are the seven rows of the plan's §2.3 manual-repair table plus the restore journal waiting for the game, that is catalog rows 2–9 of `fm-concurrency_primitives-…`; rows 1 (`journal-pending`, recoverable) and 10 (`lock-held-long`, whose held lock hides every journal finding) are left to the suite of F1 (`omad-m4-agent-surface-doctor-c6cm.6.1`, journal and lock detectors). All eight on **one** home, because the demo says "a home" and because that is the case no per-fixture suite covers.

